  "chapter": {
    "number": 5,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          "Remember, O Lord, what has happened to us: behold, and look on our reproach."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          "Our inheritance has been turned away to aliens, our houses to strangers:"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          "we are become orphans, we have no father, our mothers are as widows."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          "We have drunk our water for money; our wood is sold to us for a burden on our neck:"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          "we have been persecuted, we have laboured, we have had no rest."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          "Egypt gave the hand to us, Assur to their own satisfaction."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          "Our fathers sinned, and are not: we have borne their iniquities."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          "Servants have ruled over us: there is none to ransom us out of their hand."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          "We shall bring in our bread with danger of our lives, because of the sword of the wilderness."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          "Our skin is blackened like an oven; they are convulsed, because of the storms of famine."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          "They humbled the women in Sion, the virgins in the cities of Juda."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          "Princes were hanged up by their hands: the elders were not honored."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          "The chosen men lifted up the voice in weeping, and the youths fainted under the wood."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          "And the elders ceased from the gate, the chosen men ceased from their music."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          "The joy of our heart has ceased; our dance is turned into mourning."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          "The crown has fallen from our head: yes, woe to us! for we have sinned."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          "For this has grief come; our heart is sorrowful: for this our eyes are darkened."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          "Over the mountain of Sion, because it is made desolate, foxes have walked therein."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          "But you, O Lord, shall dwell for ever; your throne shall endure to generation and generation."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          "Therefore will you utterly forget us, and abandon us a long time?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          "Turn us, O Lord, to you, and we shall be turned; and renew our days as before."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          "For you have indeed rejected us; you have been very angry against us."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
